WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.875
- When like the show first
comes on and it says Netlix.

00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:03.964
(imitates Netlix sound effect)

00:00:03.964 --> 00:00:06.964
(electronic sounds)

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.010
(jazz music)

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.240
- Probably Gaten, because
I feel like he'd just watch

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.110
a bunch of Ken Burns documentaries

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.150
and just cloud up my feed,

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.510
make look just sad 'cause
he was watching sad stuff.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.147
You know what I mean,
and Gaten just pushes,

00:00:23.147 --> 00:00:24.010
"did you see that doc?"

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.681
I'm just like "yeah dude, it's really sad,

00:00:25.681 --> 00:00:26.514
"I don't really wanna,

00:00:26.514 --> 00:00:28.920
"I don't wanna hear about
it right now." (laughs)

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.320
He was a huge, Gaten's
just a real history buff

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.380
and a lot of history is super sad.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.120
And so sometimes he
talks, he's not a downer,

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.210
he's not as much of a downer
as I'm making him out to be,

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.330
he's like a sweet puppy dog,

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.947
but sometimes he'll say
something where I'm like

00:00:40.947 --> 00:00:42.834
"man I don't wanna hear that today."

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:43.910
(laughs) It's sad.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.240
So yeah, probably Gaten,
I would not trust that man

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:47.690
with any password in my life.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:48.960
I would trust him with like a bomb

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.630
that he had to diffuse or something,

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:51.930
'cause he's trustworthy like that.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.843
But not for a Netlix account.

00:00:53.843 --> 00:00:56.200
(beeps)

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.650
There was that show Sex
Ed, which I really liked

00:00:58.650 --> 00:00:59.730
which is on Netlix.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.563
But I'm trying to think of something

00:01:00.563 --> 00:01:01.680
that we all raved about.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.027
I remember I just saw Mid
90s, Jonah Hill's Mid 90s

00:01:04.027 --> 00:01:06.960
and I was raving about it on
set a lot and talking about it.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.460
Oh yeah, we talked about Star Wars a lot,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.750
that was the season.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.700
I remember at least five
different conversations

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:12.930
about the new Star Wars movies.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.810
(beeps)

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.350
I don't know, I liked them.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.710
I don't have any problems with them.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.350
I like episode three a lot. (laughs)

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.050
I like the lava fight at the end

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:25.300
where Anakin burns to death. (laughs)

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.011
But it's fun, I don't
know, I liked those movies.

00:01:27.011 --> 00:01:28.900
(beeps)

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.420
- Oh man, well, I had a VHS player

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.140
up until I was 10, or like nine or 10

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:37.960
and so,

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:41.060
I watched, some of the first
movies I ever watched was

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:44.560
we had a box set of
Revenge of the Sith and

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.115
A New Hope, so I watched
it really early on.

00:01:47.115 --> 00:01:49.030
(beeps)

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:50.120
Yeah, yeah, I dunno.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.060
I guess VHS was introduced earlier.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.460
I think a lot of my friends
grew up with more DVD players

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.080
but I grew up with VHS.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.350
And then moved slowly to DVD

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.383
and then Blu-ray when the PS3 came out.

00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:04.383
(beeps)

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:06.420
Yeah, definitely.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.680
I think was again, like
it was on accident,

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.350
but it makes so much sense.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:12.980
Certain things identified with me so much

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.590
just 'cause all the Duffers' influences

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.810
and all the Stranger Things influences

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:19.100
are all movies that I
grew up watching, so,

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.396
it definitely came full circle for sure.

00:02:21.396 --> 00:02:24.080
(beeps)

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.060
Ooh, Barry.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.020
I just watched Barry, finished it.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.730
Like I said before, I
watched all of Sex Ed,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.700
which I really liked, thought
it was super fun on Netflix.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.760
Yeah, Barry, I was super behind on Barry.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:34.860
I had only seen the first episode

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:37.800
then I just binge watched the first season

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:38.910
and season two now.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.144
But that was probably the
last thing I did, yeah.

00:02:41.144 --> 00:02:43.150
(beeps)

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.987
I got a text from a
bunch of friends saying

00:02:44.987 --> 00:02:46.820
"there's Bob Dylan vibes" so,

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.630
yeah they're very big compliments.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.410
I mean from music, for
sure, but style never,

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.160
or look has never been Bob Dylan,

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.430
even now that's what comes out.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:55.730
I hope I get to see that dude,

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:56.970
'cause he's getting older now.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.930
So, hope I get to see him
before he kicks the bucket,

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:00.763
one day.

00:03:00.763 --> 00:03:02.240
(beeps)

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.710
When I was younger I didn't
really have like, a set style.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:07.820
I was kind of into
skater clothes and stuff,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:11.210
so I'd just wear straight
skater stuff and baggy clothes

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.480
and then I started doing
more stuff like this,

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.420
so now I wear more like, I don't know,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.820
70s rock stuff and,

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:21.650
it's like a 70s rock with like,

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.930
skate culture vibe,

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:24.763
I've no idea.

00:03:24.763 --> 00:03:25.910
I just wear whatever I think is

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.850
cool and comfortable I guess.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.430
And like makes you feel more unique

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:31.930
because it's not as
much of a thing anymore,

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.830
but I think that look
is coming back for sure.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:38.590
There's a reason why Reebok
Classics are huge now again,

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.310
and all the vintage stuff you see,

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.090
that's why Stranger Things
has a collab with Nike now,

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.023
with the Cortez's and stuff.

00:03:43.023 --> 00:03:45.130
(beeps)

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:47.130
Whatever, I'll still throw on a t-shirt

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.640
and gross sweatpants and walk around.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.430
Crocs. (laughs)

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.610
(beeps)

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.940
I mean I would love to see myself

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.430
on a set for the first time.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.380
'Cause that was the moment that

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.103
everything clicked in my head and,

00:04:02.046 --> 00:04:03.530
it was probably the most fun I'd ever had.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.000
I'd love to go back and see that happen.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.520
I remember I was just so excited,

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.380
and I was probably, I couldn't shut up,

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.370
could not stop talking about
everything and cameras,

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.570
I was just so overstimulated.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.640
So if I were to ever go back

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.500
I'd just tell myself to shut up.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.875
And just watch and just learn.

00:04:17.875 --> 00:04:19.800
(beeps)

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.320
Dude,

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.950
Spiderverse was amazing,
the last Spiderman movie.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.630
I saw that in theaters
twice, just 'cause I,

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.210
it was something so unique.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.220
The animation was so unique

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.660
and I hadn't seen something
like that in so long.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:35.360
And it's old now, but it came
out like 10, 11 years ago

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.320
but all the old Laika stuff,

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:38.430
I haven't seen any of their new stuff

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:42.689
but Coraline and ParaNorman
and all that stuff is amazing.

00:04:42.689 --> 00:04:45.440
And occasionally I'll watch some anime.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.260
I'm not like huge into anime or anything.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.230
Fullmetal Alchemist:
Brotherhood is really good

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.832
and Gurren Lagann is great.

00:04:50.832 --> 00:04:53.440
And Akira, Akira's one of my
favorite films of all time.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.160
I don't know if that classifies as anime,

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.027
but you know, I watched it.

00:04:57.027 --> 00:04:59.210
(beeps)

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.043
Doo-doom?

00:05:00.043 --> 00:05:02.090
Like the game Doom?
(laughter in background)

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.503
Doo-doom!

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:04.940
Doo-doom!

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:05.773
Doo-doom!

